<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Terms & Conditions | LifeLine' }) %>
<section class="wrap policy-page">
  <span class="eyebrow">USING LIFELINE</span>
  <h1>Terms &amp; conditions</h1>
  <p class="policy-updated">Use LifeLine responsibly and verify all donation and transfusion decisions with qualified professionals.</p>
  <article class="policy-card">
    <h2>Coordination service only</h2>
    <p>LifeLine helps people find donor listings, submit requests and locate listed blood banks. It does not collect, test, store or supply blood and does not provide medical advice, emergency response or transfusion services.</p>
    <h2>Medical decisions and emergencies</h2>
    <p>Donor matching is preliminary and does not establish clinical compatibility or donor eligibility. Qualified medical staff must verify identity, blood type, screening and crossmatching. For an emergency, contact a hospital or local emergency service directly.</p>
    <h2>Accurate, respectful use</h2>
    <p>Provide information you are authorized to share, keep account credentials private and do not misuse donor contact details. Availability and blood bank listings can change; confirm details directly before relying on them.</p>
    <h2>Accounts and availability</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for activity under your account. Donor participation is voluntary; update or remove your availability when your circumstances change.</p>
    <h2>Service limitations</h2>
    <p>LifeLine cannot guarantee that a donor, blood group or blood bank will be available or that a request will be fulfilled. The service may be unavailable while it is maintained or updated.</p>
    <p class="policy-note">These demonstration terms are informational and are not a substitute for reviewed legal terms for a public service.</p>
  </article>
</section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
